# GUNUCO UI Implementation Document

This file is the primary implementation reference for screens, states, fields, and operational flows.

============================================================
1. CURRENT SYSTEM SCOPE
============================================================

Product: GUNUCO Multi-Category Ordering and Delivery System

Current operating model:
- One production house accepts and fulfils every order. `Pickup-at-Store` is the customer-facing label for collection there; it is not a separate store entity.
- `Owner` is the highest web-admin role with full control and final authority. `Admin` manages menu definitions and operations. `Branch Manager` is restricted to assigned locations and location-level overrides.
- Delivery Partners collect only local `Doorstep-Delivery` orders from the production house; `Pickup-at-Store` orders remain in the Admin pickup queue and NYC Cookies `Nationwide-Delivery` orders use the courier-shipment workspace.
- Top-level categories are `Cakes`, `Coffee`, `Pizza`, and `Burgers`. Only `Cakes` is active and implemented at launch; the others are seeded inactive.
- Cakes launches with `GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES`, `GUNUCO CHEESE CAKES`, `GUNUCO BROWNIES`, `GUNUCO NYC COOKIES`, `CASUAL CAKES`, `WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES`, and `OCCASIONAL CAKES`.
- `GUNUCO NYC COOKIES` alone can add Nationwide-Delivery. Admin independently controls Regular City and All-India coverage and may enable all or selected Indian states/union territories. Other subcategories cannot use this capability.
- GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES contains GUNUCO's special, curated cake catalogue. Custom Cakes remain a dedicated cake request workflow.
- Admin can add, edit, activate, deactivate, and reorder parent categories and subcategories from the Admin Panel. Coffee, Pizza, and Burgers remain hidden until configured and activated.
- Category names, hierarchy, product options, and navigation entries are configuration-driven and must not be hard-coded.
- Branch creation and transfers are feature-disabled at launch, but locations, assignments, orders, POS, fulfilment, quotas, and reporting are location-ready from the first release.

Current panels:
1. Web Admin Panel
2. Delivery Partner Panel
3. Customer Support Panel

Portal entry points:
- Owner, Admin, and Branch Manager: `https://admin.gunuco.com/login`
- Customer Support Agent: `https://support.gunuco.com/login`

Customer application identity:
- Customers browse without signing in but must authenticate before checkout.
- Login and sign-up use E.164 phone number plus SMS OTP only. Do not show password, email-login, social-login, or guest-checkout controls.
- OTP screens include phone entry, country code, code entry, resend countdown, attempt/rate-limit state, expiry, and change-number action.
- Successful first verification creates the customer account; later verification signs into the same unique phone account.
- Use 15-minute access tokens and rotating 30-day refresh sessions, with at most three active devices and token-family revocation on refresh-token reuse.
- Saved-address CRUD is account-owned. Require recipient name/phone, address line 1, city, state, postal code, latitude, and longitude; line 2, landmark, and label are optional.

