Access rule:
- Owner sees every menu item and controls branches, Global POS, admin-location assignments, global menu rules, and all role permissions.
- Admin sees operational sections and can manage categories, subcategories, products, descriptions, images, pricing, add-ons, customization, Branch Managers, and delivery partners. Owner-only actions are hidden or read-only.
- Admin has all operational Support Tickets controls: view, assign/reassign/unassign, prioritize, reply, add internal notes, own escalations, set Open/Pending, Close, and Reopen.
- Branch Manager sees assigned-location Dashboard, Point of Sale, Orders, Menu Management, Production Queue, Delivery Partners, pickup, and delivery operations. Menu definitions are read-only; location availability, stock state, and authorized location price overrides are editable.
- Delivery Partner never enters this panel.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 ADMIN DASHBOARD
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Central control for production-house orders, preparation, delivery, payments, and exceptions.

Required cards:
- Today's Orders
- Today's Revenue
- Cakes parent orders with configurable subcategory breakdowns
- Custom Cakes Orders
- Wedding & Anniversary Orders
- Awaiting Acceptance
- Preparing
- Ready for Delivery
- Deliveries Pending
- Delivering
- Delivered Today

Top controls:
- Accept Orders ON/OFF
- Active parent-category and subcategory availability controls generated from configuration
- Accept Custom Cakes ON/OFF
- Acceptance modes generated for each active parent category or subcategory
- Custom Cakes Acceptance Mode: Automatic / Manual
- Delivery Assignment Mode: Automatic / Manual

ORDER CONTROLS BOARD

The dashboard must contain a visible Order Controls board:

```text
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| ORDER CONTROLS                                                           |
| Accept Orders                         [ON/OFF]                            |
| Active Category/Subcategory           [Automatic | Manual]                |
| Custom Cakes Acceptance               [Automatic | Manual]                |
| Delivery Assignment                   [Automatic | Manual]                |
|                                                                          |
| DAILY LIMITS                                                             |
| All Orders                            [Current / Limit] [Edit Limit]      |
| Each Active Category/Subcategory      [Current / Limit] [Edit Limit]      |
| Custom Cakes                          [Current / Limit] [Edit Limit]      |
|                                                                          |
| Wedding/Anniversary Window            [72h minimum | 720h maximum]       |
| Eligible Cakes Subcategories          [ON/OFF] [Cutoff] [Slots]          |
| Fulfilment Methods       [Pickup-at-Store ON] [Doorstep-Delivery ON]     |
| Quota Reset                           [Midnight, configured timezone]     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Control behavior:
- Automatic: accept a valid order immediately after availability, payment, requested quantity, delivery time, and every applicable daily limit pass validation.
- Manual: create the order as Not Accepted and place it in Awaiting Acceptance for Admin action.
- Admin can manually Accept or Reject an order waiting in Manual mode.
- Changing mode affects new orders only; it must not silently change existing orders.
- Global OFF overrides every acceptance mode and category.
- Daily limits are numeric values greater than zero and remain editable by Admin.
- Show live accepted quantity, configured limit, percentage used, and remaining capacity.
- Alert Admin at 80 percent usage and block acceptance when the requested quantity would exceed a limit.
- Reset daily usage at midnight in the configured production house timezone.
- `WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES` orders require a requested fulfilment time at least 72 hours and at most 720 hours after server order-creation time.
- Reject this subcategory before payment when the requested time is earlier than 72 hours or later than 720 hours. Exactly 72 and exactly 720 hours are allowed.
- This fixed 3-to-30-day window applies only to `WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES`; no other category or Custom Cake request inherits it.

Delivery controls and visibility:
- Deliveries Pending counts orders with delivery status `Pending Assignment` or `Assigned`.
- Delivering counts orders with delivery status `Picked Up` or `Out for Delivery`.
- Delivered Today counts orders marked `Delivered` today.
- Dashboard and Orders tables show the assigned delivery partner name beside delivery status.
- Automatic assignment starts when an accepted order needs delivery; the rider is notified immediately and can view the future pickup time while production continues.
- Automatic assignment selects an Active and Online rider who accepts deliveries, has no conflicting pickup, serves the delivery area, and has the lowest active workload. Rating and distance break ties.
- The selected rider must accept within the configured timeout. Rejection or timeout automatically tries the next eligible rider.
- If no rider accepts, status remains `Pending Assignment` and Admin receives an alert.
- Manual mode leaves the order Pending Assignment until Admin selects a rider.
- Admin can override or reassign before pickup. Every attempt and reassignment is recorded.
- Automatic rider assignment runs only for `Doorstep-Delivery`; `Pickup-at-Store` never creates a rider assignment.

Customer fulfilment options:
- Before payment, the customer chooses exactly one currently eligible method: `Pickup-at-Store`, local `Doorstep-Delivery`, or NYC Cookies-only `Nationwide-Delivery` when enabled for the verified destination state/UT.
- `Pickup-at-Store`: customer collects from the production house and delivery fee is always Rs 0.
- `Doorstep-Delivery`: customer enters an address and the server calculates road distance from the production house.
- Cakes and eligible Cakes subcategory doorstep fee: up to 5 km inclusive = Rs 0; over 5 km through 8 km = Rs 39; over 8 km through 10 km = Rs 59; over 10 km through 15 km = Rs 159.
- `Doorstep-Delivery` beyond 15 km is unavailable by default; show `Pickup-at-Store` or ask the customer to choose an address within range.
- Custom Cakes offer both `Pickup-at-Store` and `Doorstep-Delivery`, and both have Rs 0 delivery fee regardless of distance within the configured service area.
- Recalculate and display `Subtotal - Discount + Delivery Fee = Payable Total` immediately whenever the customer changes the option or doorstep address.
- Show the selected option, verified distance, delivery fee, address or store pickup instructions, selected time, and final payable total on the checkout review before enabling payment.
- Do not book a catalogue order until the customer reviews the recalculated total and completes verified full payment. A Custom Cake request may be saved before payment for clarification, feasibility review, and quoting, but cannot enter production until the quote is approved and full payment is captured.
- Pickup lifecycle is `Pickup Scheduled -> Ready for Pickup -> Collected`.
- Customer-facing Order ID format is `YY-N`, with a minimum two-digit sequence: `26-01`, `26-02`, ... `26-888`. The sequence restarts at `01` each calendar year.
- Admin marks pickup orders Ready for Pickup. Authorized Owner, Admin, Branch Manager, and POS order views may display the Order ID, but the pickup-validation input remains blank. At collection, staff asks the customer to state the Order ID and the server validates an exact match before enabling `Confirm Collection` or `Collected`.
- At the doorstep, the delivery partner sees order details except all Order ID fields, calls or asks the customer for the Order ID, enters that customer-provided value, and receives only a privacy-safe success or failure before `Delivered` can be enabled.
- No OTP or separate pickup code is used for either fulfilment option.
- Record who validated the Order ID, when it was validated, and whether validation occurred at the store or doorstep.
- Generate the yearly sequence atomically so simultaneous orders cannot receive duplicate IDs.
- Store collection/delivery completion and successful validation in one server transaction. Store validation is limited to an Owner, Admin, or Branch Manager authorized for the order's location; doorstep validation is limited to the assigned rider.
- Validate the exact customer-facing Order ID only. OTP, pickup code, phone number, or a client-submitted success value cannot substitute for the server comparison.
- Rate-limit failed entries and alert Admin about repeated mismatches.
- Customer receives the Order ID, pickup address, map link, operating hours, and Ready for Pickup notification.

Cashless payment rules:
- Never offer Cash, Cash on Delivery, or cash payment at the store or doorstep.
- Capture the complete server-calculated payable total online before booking every catalogue, custom-cake, same-day, application, or POS order.
- Do not provide advance, deposit, installment, balance-due, pay-later, or partial-booking controls.
- An unpaid Custom Cake request may remain pending for clarification and quoting but cannot enter production.
- Reserve quota and any same-day slot only when the gateway-verified captured amount equals the current payable total.
- If the captured amount differs from the current total, do not partially book the order; reconcile the payment and require a fresh full-payment attempt where applicable.
- Admin sees payable amount, amount paid, payment status, payment attempts, and gateway-confirmation alerts.
- Delivery Partners see payment clearance status but never receive or record cash.

Same-day delivery controls:
- Same-day delivery applies only to eligible Cakes subcategories. `WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES` is never same-day eligible because its minimum lead time is 72 hours.
- Admin controls same-day ON/OFF independently for each eligible Cakes subcategory.
- Admin sets the order cutoff time, minimum preparation lead time, same-day slot capacity, delivery slots, and service area.
- Each cake has an Allow Same-Day Delivery ON/OFF override.
- Same-day is offered only when global/category/product acceptance is ON, the cake supports it, the cutoff has not passed, preparation can finish before the selected slot, daily quotas have capacity, a delivery slot is available, and the address is serviceable.
- If same-day is unavailable, show the next available date or slot instead of accepting an impossible delivery time.

Quick actions:
- Add Cake
- Manage Categories
- Add Add-On
- Review Custom Cake
- Assign Delivery
- Create Offer

Recent orders columns:
- Order ID
- Parent Category
- Subcategory
- Customer
- Requested Delivery
- Amount
- Production Status
- Delivery Status
- Assigned Delivery Partner

Critical rule:
- If global Accept Orders is OFF, no new order from any category, subcategory, or Custom Cake workflow can be accepted.
- Passing validation in Automatic mode changes status directly to Accepted.
- Passing validation in Manual mode leaves status as Not Accepted until Admin accepts it.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.1A POINT OF SALE
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Provide assisted, cashless Pickup-at-Store ordering only when a customer at an authorized location cannot reasonably use the application.

Use a Zepto-style category-browsing POS experience optimized for repeated cashier operation; this is an operational POS, not a simplified order form.

Access and controls:
- Owner, Admin, or Branch Manager may use POS only at an authorized location where Global POS and Location POS are both ON.
- Resolve location from the authenticated assignment; do not provide an unrestricted location selector.
- Require an exception reason: No mobile device, Device unavailable, Application unavailable, or Accessibility assistance.
- Mobile number may be omitted only for No mobile device, which requires a printed receipt.

Workspace:
- Use a stable three-column desktop layout: dynamic category rail on the left, selected-category product grid in the center, and persistent cart on the right.
- Keep category rail and cart fixed while the product workspace scrolls. At narrower widths collapse the rail; below 1024px use a category side sheet and full-height cart sheet.
- Generate top-level categories and expandable subcategories from active location configuration in display order. Show Cakes and its seven active subcategories at launch; hide inactive Coffee, Pizza, and Burgers.
- Selecting a parent shows products across active descendants. Selecting a subcategory updates the center grid without a full page reload and keeps the selected state visible.
- Product header contains category name, count, search, Available Only toggle, and Display Order/Name/Price sort.
- Product cards use stable dimensions and show image, name, starting/current price, availability, same-day state, and remaining quota.
- A fixed-option product adds its effective Default Quantity immediately. A product with enabled customization or add-ons opens a compact configuration drawer over the product workspace.
- Render only effective customization controls: flavour, Egg/Eggless, sweetener, flour, size/weight, add-ons, and quantity.
- Search by product name or code within the selected category, with All Active Categories scope. Scanner/SKU input uses product-code lookup.
- Persist active and held POS carts server-side. Restore the active cart after refresh or reconnect.
- Cart lines show product, selected options/add-ons, unit price, quantity stepper, line total, edit, and remove. Merge only identical configurations.
- Provide Clear, Hold, Resume, and Abandon actions. Held carts remain scoped to operator and location unless transferred by an authorized role.
- Show Saved, Syncing, Offline, and conflict states. On stale row-version updates retain the latest server cart and require Review Cart.
- Subscribe to location-scoped category, product, price, customization, add-on, offer, quota, and availability events with polling fallback. Refetch affected records; never trust pushed prices.
- Requote affected lines and mark Price Changed, Unavailable, Quota Exceeded, or Configuration Changed. Preserve lines for review and disable payment until resolved.
- Cart summary shows customer details, required pickup time, itemized options/add-ons, offer, subtotal, discount, tax, and full payable total.
- Fixed Pickup-at-Store fulfilment; POS never creates doorstep delivery.
- Require verified full payment using Card, UPI, or Net Banking at launch. Keep Wallet and Store Credit hidden and unavailable until a later release. Never show advance, installment, balance, Cash, COD, Record Cash, or manual Mark Paid.
- Show payment pending, gateway confirmation, success, failure, and retry states. Client-side gateway success never books an order.
- Receipt preview provides Print Receipt, Share Receipt, New Sale, and View Order.

After verified full payment and all server checks, atomically convert the POS cart into one Accepted order in the shared production queue, consume quota, preserve cart/order linkage, and record channel, location, operator, exception reason, and idempotency key. Reusing a converted cart returns the existing order. Failed or abandoned payments do not consume quota or generate a paid receipt.

