------------------------------------------------------------
3.2A WEDDING & ANNIVERSARY ORDERS
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Provide a dedicated Admin queue for every order whose subcategory is `WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES`, while retaining the same records in the main Orders page and production queue.

Access:
- Owner and Admin see all authorized records. Branch Manager sees assigned-location records only.
- This is a filtered operational view, not a separate order type or lifecycle.

Required summary cards:
- Scheduled in Next 3 Days
- Scheduled in Next 7 Days
- Awaiting Acceptance
- Preparing
- Ready for Pickup/Delivery
- At-Risk Orders

Required filters and columns:
- Requested fulfilment date range, order date, location, status, fulfilment method, product, customer, payment status, and production status
- Order ID, order-created time, requested fulfilment time, lead time remaining, customer, product, configured options, quantity, amount, payment, production, fulfilment, assigned rider, and actions

Rules and actions:
- Default sort is requested fulfilment time ascending, then order-created time ascending.
- Show `Too Early` when requested time is below 72 hours and `Too Far` when above 720 hours; block quote/payment/order creation for either state.
- Show a live countdown and At Risk when remaining preparation time is below the configured operational threshold.
- Provide View, Accept/Reject where permitted, Update Production Status, Assign/Reassign Delivery Partner, and Cancel when eligible.
- Do not allow changing the requested time outside the original inclusive 72-to-720-hour window measured from the immutable order-created time.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.3 MENU MANAGEMENT
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Provide one Zomato-style workspace for entering and maintaining the complete menu category-wise and subcategory-wise without moving between separate screens.

Workspace layout:
- Left category tree: searchable parent categories with expandable subcategories, product counts, status, drag-to-reorder, Add Category, and Add Subcategory.
- Center product list/grid: products for the selected category or subcategory with image, name, short description, price, discount price, customization summary, add-ons, availability, and display order.
- Right product editor drawer: create, edit, duplicate, preview, publish, deactivate, or archive a product without leaving the selected category.
- Sticky top actions: Add Product, Bulk Import, Export, Reorder, Preview Customer Menu, and Save Drafts.
- Tabs inside Menu Management: Products, Categories, Add-Ons, Customization, Pricing & Weights, and Location Availability.
- Breadcrumb always shows `Menu > Parent Category > Subcategory`; Add Product preselects the currently selected category and subcategory.
- Preserve filters, selected category, scroll position, and unsaved drafts when switching tabs or products.

Product entry fields:
- Product code/SKU, product name, short description, full description, primary image, optional gallery images, parent category, subcategory, food type/tags, base price, discount price, tax class, preparation time, display order, featured state, same-day eligibility, daily quota, and Available ON/OFF.
- Show category-specific customization, sizes/weights, add-ons, and price rows only when applicable to the selected category module.
- Product preview displays the exact customer card and detail view before publishing.
- Save Draft permits incomplete records; Publish requires category, name, description, image, valid price, location availability, and complete pricing for every enabled required option.
- Duplicate copies product content and options but generates a new product code and starts as Draft/Unavailable.

Permission behavior:
- Owner and Admin can create and edit categories, subcategories, products, descriptions, images, pricing, options, add-ons, assignments, and display order.
- Branch Manager can view the complete menu for assigned locations and update only location availability, sold-out state, quota, and authorized location price overrides.
- Every create, update, publish, reorder, archive, bulk import, and override records actor, role, timestamp, before/after values, and location where applicable.

Table columns:
- Image
- Cake Name
- Parent Category: Cakes
- Subcategory: one of the seven configured Cakes subcategories
- Effective customization summary
- Available values for enabled Flavour, Egg, Sweetener, Flour, and Size/Weight controls
- Starting Price
- Orders Today
- Daily Quota
- Availability
- Edit

Add/Edit Cake fields:
- Cake Name
- Description
- Product Image
- Parent Category: Cakes
- Configurable Subcategory
- Per-product Flavour, Egg Preference, Sweetener Type, Flour Type, and Size/Weight control: Inherit / ON / OFF
- Per-product Quantity control: Inherit / Override; Override requires Minimum, Maximum, and Default Quantity
- Available values and defaults for each effectively enabled customization
- Effective Default Quantity, initially inherited as 1 unless Admin overrides it
- Base Price
- Option Price Adjustments
- Discount Price
- Applicable Add-Ons and assignment preview
- Preparation Time
- Allow Same-Day Delivery ON/OFF
- Daily Quantity Quota
- Featured ON/OFF
- Available ON/OFF

Automatic price controls:
- Admin sets the base price for each cake.
- Admin manages an Ingredient Pricing Matrix for enabled customization types only.
- The matrix stores one editable 1kg price contribution for each enabled Flavour, Egg/Eggless, Sweetener, and Flour option.
- For every weight, calculate the option contribution as `1kg Price Contribution x (Selected Weight in Grams / 1000)`; 500g uses a multiplier of `0.5`.
- Weight availability and the cake's base price for each sellable weight remain separately configurable.
- Admin can set a positive, zero, or negative ingredient price contribution for every selectable value.
- The customer sees the price and ingredient breakdown update immediately after every ingredient or quantity change; no Submit button is required to preview the new price.
- Formula: `Unit Price = Weight Base Price + sum of each enabled selected option's 1kg contribution x weight in kg`, where `weight in kg = selected grams / 1000`.
- `Items Total = Unit Price x Quantity`.
- `Order Total = Items Total - Discount + Delivery Fee + Tax`, where configured.
- The server recalculates the final price from current admin rules before payment; client-submitted totals are never trusted.
- The order stores the selected ingredient names, IDs, individual price contributions, pricing rule version, calculation time, and final price so later admin changes do not alter an existing order.

Default menu configuration:
- When a customer opens a customizable cake, preselect configured defaults for enabled controls and the effective Default Quantity.
- The cake's own flavour remains selected by default; if a cake supports multiple flavours, Admin chooses its default flavour.
- The catalogue `Starting Price` is the live server-calculated price for the default combination.
- Starting Price is the base plus enabled default-option contributions. Admin may change defaults, but publishing is blocked if an enabled group lacks an active default or complete pricing.
- Customer can change only enabled options and quantity. Every change recalculates the price immediately.
- A `Reset to Default` action restores the cake's configured default combination.

Customer price breakdown example:

```text
Chocolate Cake 500g Base                    Rs 500
Chocolate Flavour (500g)                    + Rs 40
Eggless (500g)                              + Rs 150
Mishri (500g)                               + Rs 40
Wheat Flour (500g)                          + Rs 150
---------------------------------------------------
Unit Price                                  Rs 880
Quantity: 2
Items Total                               Rs 1,760
```

Ingredient Pricing Matrix fields:
- Cake
- Ingredient Group: Flavour / Egg Preference / Sweetener Type / Flour Type
- Ingredient Option
- Editable 1kg Price Contribution
- Read-only calculated previews: 500g / 2kg / 3kg / selected Custom Cake weight
- Available ON/OFF
- Effective From
- Updated By
- Updated At

Pricing behavior:
- Selecting, deselecting, or replacing any ingredient triggers a fresh quote.
- Changing quantity multiplies the newly calculated unit price.
- Unavailable ingredient combinations cannot be selected or quoted.
- Checkout requests a final server quote and rejects stale or tampered pricing.
- Existing paid or accepted orders retain their stored pricing snapshot.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.3B MENU MANAGEMENT: CATEGORIES TAB
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Allow Owner and Admin to manage the customer menu hierarchy inside Menu Management without code or navigation changes. Branch Manager has read-only definition access.

Hierarchy table columns:
- Expand/collapse
- Category Code
- Display Name
- Parent Category
- Module/Type
- Status
- Display Order
- Active Locations
- Product Count
- Updated By and Updated At
- Actions

Actions:
- Add Parent Category
- Add Subcategory
- Edit
- Activate or Deactivate
- Reorder
- View Products
- Configure Customization
- Configure Locations

Create/edit fields:
- Unique code
- Display name
- Optional parent
- Description and image
- Category module/type
- Display order
- Acceptance mode
- Daily quota
- Same-day eligibility
- Active/Inactive status

Rules:
- Seed Cakes active with GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES, GUNUCO CHEESE CAKES, GUNUCO BROWNIES, GUNUCO NYC COOKIES, CASUAL CAKES, WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES, and OCCASIONAL CAKES.
- Seed Coffee, Pizza, and Burgers inactive. They appear only after their catalogue and operating rules are configured and activated.
- Configure Customization is available only in the web Admin Panel to Owner and Admin. Branch Manager sees configured/effective values read-only.
- Main-category rows provide explicit ON/OFF switches for Flavour Type, Egg or Eggless, Sweetener Type, Flour Type, and Size or Weight.
- Subcategory rows provide Inherit, ON, or OFF for every customization type. Inherit resolves from the parent main category.
- Product controls provide Inherit, ON, or OFF. Inherit resolves from the effective subcategory, or directly from the main category for a direct child product.
- Effective state is Product explicit ON/OFF, then Subcategory explicit ON/OFF, then Main Category ON/OFF, otherwise OFF.
- Resolve each option independently. A product configured with only Sweetener Type ON and Flavour, Egg/Eggless, Flour Type, and Size/Weight OFF renders only Sweetener Type and Quantity in customer and POS forms.
- Do not provide a blanket customization switch. Admin enables only the groups needed at each category, subcategory, or product. ON means applicable and requires a valid selection, OFF means hidden and server-rejected when submitted, and Inherit uses the nearest explicit parent setting.
- Quantity uses separate hierarchy controls: main-category Override and subcategory/product Inherit or Override. Override requires Minimum Quantity, Maximum Quantity, and Default Quantity.
- Resolve quantity as Product → Subcategory → Main Category → minimum 1, maximum 99, default 1. Quantity is mandatory and cannot be turned OFF.
- Require minimum greater than zero, maximum at least minimum, and default inside the range. Enforce boundaries in customer/POS steppers and on the server.
- Show Configured State, Effective State, and Source (`Product`, `Subcategory`, or `Main Category`) for every control.
- Launch defaults are OFF for GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES, GUNUCO CHEESE CAKES, GUNUCO BROWNIES, and GUNUCO NYC COOKIES.
- Launch defaults are ON for CASUAL CAKES, WEDDING OR ANNIVERSARY CAKES, and OCCASIONAL CAKES.
- Before enabling Flavour, Egg/Eggless, Sweetener, or Flour, require at least one active value, a default, and one 1kg price contribution for every active value. Before enabling Size/Weight, require at least one active weight with its separate weight base price. Disabled controls are hidden and rejected by the server.
- Before saving a main-category or subcategory change, show affected inherited descendants; explicit child overrides remain unchanged.
- Saving emits a catalogue-change event and requotes affected customer and POS carts. Completed order snapshots remain unchanged.
- Prevent selecting the current category or a descendant as its parent.
- Block destructive deletion when products or child categories depend on the record; use deactivation to preserve history.
- Deactivating a parent blocks new activity for descendants but preserves products and historical orders.
- Global activation does not automatically enable a category at every location.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.3C MENU MANAGEMENT: ADD-ONS TAB
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Allow Admin to configure additional selectable or required items and pricing from the Admin Panel. Owner has full authority; Branch Manager can only view and sell available add-ons at assigned locations.

List columns:
- Add-On
- Description
- Price
- Required/Optional
- Minimum and Maximum Quantity
- Category/Subcategory/Product Assignments
- Active Locations
- Status
- Actions

Add/edit fields:
- Unique code
- Name
- Description
- Price
- Required or Optional
- Minimum quantity
- Maximum quantity
- Display order
- Available ON/OFF
- Parent-category assignments
- Subcategory assignments
- Product assignments
- Location availability
- Optional location price override

Rules:
- Require at least one category, subcategory, or product assignment.
- Required add-ons have a minimum quantity of at least 1.
- Maximum quantity cannot be below minimum quantity; price cannot be negative.
- Customer and POS product forms show applicable add-ons after product options.
- Changing an add-on requests a fresh server quote and updates its itemized unit price, quantity, and total.
- Disable unavailable add-ons with a reason and remove stale selections after re-quote.
- Save add-on name, description, unit price, quantity, required status, and total as immutable order-time snapshots.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.3D MENU MANAGEMENT: PRICING & WEIGHTS TAB
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Provide one Admin section for entering every ingredient and weight price used by dynamic quotes.

Tabs:
- Flavour Pricing
- Egg/Eggless Pricing
- Flour Type Pricing
- Sweetener Type Pricing
- Weight Pricing
- Price Preview

Common pricing-table columns:
- Cake or Apply-to-All Cakes
- Category/Subcategory generated from active configuration, plus Custom Cakes
- Option Name
- Calculated 500g Preview
- Editable 1kg Price Contribution
- Calculated 2kg Preview
- Calculated 3kg Preview
- Available ON/OFF
- Effective From
- Updated By
- Updated At

Default controls:
- Default option radio button for each ingredient group
- Default Weight, initially 500g
- Default Quantity, initially 1
- Starting Price preview
- Lowest-default validation result

Initial defaults for catalogue cakes:
- Sugar Type: Mishri
- Egg Preference: Egg
- Flour Type: Maida
- Weight: 500g
- Quantity: 1

Admin can later change a cake's default selections. Before saving, the system verifies every default is active for that cake and weight and that the default combination is the lowest available starting-price combination.

Weight Pricing tab:

```text
| Weight | Catalogue Cakes | Custom Cakes | Weight Base Price | Available |
| 500 g  | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]          | [ON/OFF]  |
| 1 kg   | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]          | [ON/OFF]  |
| 2 kg   | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]          | [ON/OFF]  |
| 3 kg   | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]          | [ON/OFF]  |
| 4-10kg | No              | Yes          | [amount]          | [ON/OFF]  |
| >10 kg | No              | Request Only | Manual Quote      | [ON/OFF]  |
```

Weight rules:
- Customizable catalogue cakes use configured weights from 500g through 3kg; fixed-size products hide the weight selector.
- Custom Cakes use configured weights from 500g through 10kg.
- Admin may enable or disable each supported weight and set its weight base price separately from 1kg customization-option contributions.
- For a Custom Cake above 10kg, customer selects `Above 10kg`, enters the required weight, and submits a quote request.
- Above-10kg requests cannot receive an automatic final price or automatic acceptance.
- Admin reviews production feasibility, delivery handling, lead time, and price, then sends a manual quote.
- Customer must approve the quote before payment and production.
- Quantity means the number of cakes; weight means the weight of each cake. Keep these as separate fields.

Catalogue ingredient pricing example. Only the 1kg column is editable; other values are calculated previews:

```text
| Ingredient Group | Option      | 500g Preview | 1kg Editable | 2kg Preview | 3kg Preview |
| Sugar Type       | Mishri      | +40  | +80 | +160| +240|
| Sugar Type       | Stevia      | +60  | +120| +240| +360|
| Flour Type       | Maida       | +100 | +200| +400| +600|
| Flour Type       | Wheat Flour | +150 | +300| +600| +900|
| Egg Preference   | Egg         | +100 | +200| +400| +600|
| Egg Preference   | Eggless     | +150 | +300| +600| +900|
```

Custom Cake 1kg pricing basis:
- Admin enters the base and all enabled customization contributions for 1kg only.
- For 500g through 10kg, calculate each contribution as `1kg Price Contribution x (Requested Weight in Grams / 1000)`.
- Example: a 1kg Wheat Flour contribution of Rs 300 becomes Rs 1,500 for a 5kg Custom Cake because the multiplier is 5.
- Admin can override the calculated quote for design complexity, structure, decoration, or special handling and must enter an override reason.
- Above 10kg always remains a manual quote.
- The customer sees both the calculated 1kg-based amount and any approved manual adjustment.
- For unpaid requests use Approve Quote, Request Clarification, or Reject. Approve Quote never marks the order Accepted; only customer quote approval plus verified full payment accepts it for production.

Price Preview:
- Admin selects a cake, flavour, Egg/Eggless, flour type, sugar type, weight, and quantity.
- Show the same itemized dynamic price breakdown that the customer will see.
- Prevent publishing a cake if no active price exists for a required option or allowed weight.
- For catalogue cakes, preview uses the selected weight's base price plus each enabled option's 1kg contribution multiplied by the selected weight in kg.
- For Custom Cakes, preview shows the 1kg basis, weight multiplier, and manual adjustment separately.

Quota rules:
- Stop accepting the cake when its daily quantity quota is reached.
- Show an alert at 80 percent utilization.
- Reset usage at midnight in the production house timezone.

GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES rules:
- Owner and Admin can add a cake to or remove a cake from GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES; Branch Manager cannot.
- Launch customization defaults are OFF. Admin may enable controls for the subcategory or override individual products later.
- Display a visible GUNUCO PREMIUM badge in the customer catalogue, admin tables, production queue, and orders.
- Premium availability and daily limits are controlled independently from other Cakes subcategories and Custom Cakes.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.4 CUSTOM CAKES
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Review, price, accept, and produce customer-configured cakes.

Request fields:
- Customer Name
- Mobile Number
- Email
- Fulfilment Method: Pickup-at-Store, Doorstep-Delivery, or NYC Cookies-only Nationwide-Delivery
- Delivery Address (required for Doorstep-Delivery and Nationwide-Delivery)
- Destination State/UT, Coverage Mode, Shipping Fee, and Delivery-Day Range snapshots for Nationwide-Delivery
- Flavour (required)
- Egg Preference: Egg or Eggless (required)
- Sugar Type (required)
- Flour Type: Maida or Wheat Flour (required)
- Size/Weight (required)
- Requested Custom Weight in kg (shown only for Above 10kg)
- Quantity stepper (required, minimum 1)
- Occasion or Theme
- Reference Image
- Cake Message
- Special Instructions
- Requested Delivery Date and Time
- Quoted Price
- Payment Method (selected when a payable final quote is available)
- Payment Status (pre-payment requests remain Pending)

Admin actions:
- Accept
- Request Clarification
- Reject with Reason
- Confirm Price
- Move to Production
- Assign Delivery Partner when ready

Validation rules:
- Block submission when flavour, egg preference, sugar type, flour type, size, or quantity is missing.
- Custom Cake scheduling uses separately configured availability and feasibility rules; it does not inherit the Wedding or Anniversary Cakes 72-to-720-hour window.
- Standard Custom Cake weights up to 10kg can use automatic ingredient pricing.
- Above-10kg requests require Admin feasibility review and manual quote approval before acceptance.
- Enforce the daily Custom Cakes quota.
- Show the customer a clear reason when a request cannot be submitted.

Custom cake statuses:
- Not Accepted
- Clarification Requested
- Rejected
- Accepted
- Preparing
- Packed
- Ready for Delivery
- Assigned
- Picked Up
- Out for Delivery
- Delivered
- Cancelled

------------------------------------------------------------
3.5 PRODUCTION QUEUE
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Manage preparation for all production-enabled categories and subcategories in one queue.

Required columns:
- Order ID
- Parent Category
- Subcategory
- Product or Theme
- Configured Options and Add-Ons
- Quantity
- Required By
- Status
- Actions

Actions:
- Start Preparing
- Mark Packed
- Mark Ready for Pickup for Pickup-at-Store
- Mark Ready for Delivery for Doorstep-Delivery

Sort priority:
1. Requested delivery time
2. Custom cake lead-time risk
3. Accepted time

------------------------------------------------------------
3.6 DELIVERY PARTNERS
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Manage rider availability and production-house delivery assignments.

Required columns:
- Partner Name
- Mobile Number
- Vehicle Number
- Online Status
- Active Order
- Completed Today
- Rating
- Damage Incidents
- Actions

Assignment rule:
- Pickup location is always the production house.

Automatic assignment rules:
- Admin chooses Automatic or Manual assignment in the dashboard/settings.
- Automatic assignment runs after order acceptance and reserves the rider for the requested pickup window.
- Only Active, Online, Accept Deliveries ON riders are eligible.
- Prefer the lowest active workload, then shortest production-house distance, then highest rating.
- Send the assignment to one rider at a time.
- On rejection or timeout, offer it to the next eligible rider.
- After all eligible riders fail, alert Admin and keep the delivery Pending Assignment.
- Admin can manually assign or reassign any order before Picked Up.
- Once Picked Up, reassignment requires an exception reason.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.6A DELIVERY & PICKUP SETTINGS
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Give Admin full control over customer fulfilment methods, distance bands, fees, and pickup instructions.

Controls:
- Pickup-at-Store ON/OFF
- Doorstep-Delivery ON/OFF
- Pickup Address, map pin, operating hours, instructions, and contact number
- Distance Provider and Route Calculation status
- Maximum Doorstep Distance
- Custom Cakes Delivery Fee Exempt ON/OFF (default ON)
- Distance-band table with Add/Edit/Disable actions

Default distance bands for the Cakes parent and eligible Cakes subcategories:

```text
| From Distance | To Distance | Boundary Rule | Fee    | Status |
| 0 km          | 5 km        | <= 5 km       | Rs 0   | Active |
| 5 km          | 8 km        | >5 to <=8 km  | Rs 39  | Active |
| 8 km          | 10 km       | >8 to <=10 km | Rs 59  | Active |
| 10 km         | 15 km       | >10 to <=15km | Rs 159 | Active |
```

Rules:
- Use server-side road-route distance, not customer-entered distance or straight-line distance.
- Round only for display; select the fee band using the unrounded provider distance.
- Save distance, origin/destination coordinates, fee rule, fee amount, and calculation time on the order.
- If route calculation fails, do not guess a fee; ask customer to retry or choose pickup.
- Admin can change future fee rules, but existing orders retain their saved fee snapshot.
- `Pickup-at-Store` orders require no customer delivery address, distance calculation, delivery partner, or delivery fee.
- `Doorstep-Delivery` orders require a validated address and coordinates.
- Custom Cake doorstep delivery remains free, but serviceability and scheduling checks still apply.
- Pickup queue columns: Order ID, Customer, Phone, Category, Pickup Time, Pickup Status, Collected By, Validation Status, and Actions.

NYC Cookies-only delivery coverage:
- Render this card only when the selected subcategory code is `GUNUCO_NYC_COOKIES`.
- Owner and Admin edit; Branch Manager sees effective values read-only.
- Regular City Delivery ON/OFF uses existing road-distance serviceability, fees, slots, and local delivery partners.
- All-India Delivery ON/OFF exposes All States & UTs or Selected States & UTs.
- Selected mode has searchable state/UT multi-select, Select All, Clear All, enabled count, per-row ON/OFF, and changed-state summary before Save.
- Require Nationwide Shipping Fee, Minimum Delivery Days, and Maximum Delivery Days when All India is ON.
- Require at least one delivery toggle ON; require at least one state/UT in Selected mode.
- Defaults: Regular City ON; All India OFF.
- Saving requotes affected unpaid carts. Paid orders retain state, coverage mode, shipping fee, and delivery-window snapshots.
- Nationwide orders create courier shipments and never enter local delivery-partner assignment.
- POS remains Pickup-at-Store only.
- Delivery coverage does not alter customization. NYC Cookies continues to use independent category/subcategory/product Inherit/ON/OFF controls, and Admin enables only the customization groups required for each product.

Nationwide shipment workspace:
- Filter to NYC Cookies Nationwide-Delivery orders only.
- Columns: Order ID, Customer, State/UT, Items, Quantity, Shipping Fee, Delivery Window, Carrier, Tracking Number, Estimated Delivery Date, Status, Updated At, Actions.
- Statuses: Pending Dispatch, Booked, Dispatched, In Transit, Out for Delivery, Delivered, Delivery Failed, Returned, Cancelled.
- Require carrier and tracking number from Booked onward; require dispatch time from Dispatched onward; require delivered time before Delivered.
- Marking the shipment Delivered is required before the order can become Delivered.
- Local delivery partners never receive nationwide assignments.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.7 OFFERS AND DISCOUNTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Offer fields:
- Offer Name
- Discount Type
- Discount Value
- Scope: Parent Category, Subcategory, or Selected Products; add-on scope is deferred
- Start Date and Time
- End Date and Time
- Maximum Usage Count
- Available ON/OFF
- Server-calculated preview
- No stacking control. Automatically apply the single best eligible offer and show why it won.
- Add-on offer scope is deferred at launch.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.7A CUSTOMER FEEDBACK
------------------------------------------------------------

Customer experience:
- After an authenticated customer's order reaches Collected or Delivered, create one feedback request for that order.
- Launch defaults: send the initial request after 24 hours, disable the optional single reminder until configured, and expire the request after 168 hours. Always expose the same request in the application notification center.
- Opening the request shows order ID, completion date, one text-only message field, consent checkbox, Submit, and Not Now. Do not show image or file upload.
- Do not show stars, numeric scores, reactions, per-product comments, or public posting controls.
- Permit one submission per completed order. The customer may edit or withdraw it while moderation status is Pending.
- No separate public-use consent is required to submit private service feedback. A separate optional testimonial-consent checkbox controls public display in the application and static website.

Admin table:
- Feedback ID, Order ID, Customer, Message excerpt, Submitted At, Consent, Moderation Status, Moderator, and Actions
- Filter by Pending, Approved, Rejected, or Withdrawn; search by order ID or customer phone.
- Actions: View, Approve, Reject, Withdraw, and Create Testimonial when approved with active consent.

Rules:
- Only completed orders owned by the authenticated customer are eligible.
- Store push/in-app delivery and open timestamps independently from the feedback submission.
- Moderate feedback text before any public use. Rejection requires an internal reason and never deletes the audit record.
- Customer feedback is order-level message feedback only and is never converted into product ratings or aggregate stars.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.7B TESTIMONIALS
------------------------------------------------------------

Admin creates a testimonial only from approved feedback that has explicit public testimonial consent.

Fields:
- Source Feedback and Order ID, read-only
- Customer Display Name
- Approved Quote
- Approved Image
- Placement: Customer App, Static Website, or Both
- Display Order
- Active From and Active To
- Active ON/OFF

Rules:
- The approved quote may shorten the source message without changing its meaning. Keep the source feedback immutable.
- Require an approved image before publishing. Do not synthesize a rating or display stars.
- Customer consent withdrawal immediately deactivates all linked testimonials.
- Application and static website render the same API-backed ordered image carousel, excluding inactive, expired, withdrawn, or unapproved records.
- Carousel includes previous/next controls, position indicators, swipe support, pause on hover/focus, keyboard operation, alt text, and no automatic motion when reduced motion is requested.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.8 CANCEL ORDERS
------------------------------------------------------------

Cancellation fields:
- Order ID
- Current Status
- Cancellation Reason
- Internal Notes
- Original Amount
- Deduction Amount and Reason
- Refund Amount
- Notify by SMS
- Notify by Email

Rules:
- Customer cancellation uses elapsed server time from confirmed booking payment, not production status.
- Default 0 through 30 minutes: cancellation allowed with 100 percent refund of captured amount.
- Default after 30 through 60 minutes: cancellation allowed with 50 percent refund of captured amount.
- After 60 minutes: customer cancellation unavailable; show Raise Support Ticket.
- `Preparing` remains an internal production status and does not change cancellation eligibility.
- `Out for Delivery` and `Delivered` are never customer-cancellable.
- Refund base is the verified full payment captured. Refund delivery fee when delivery has not started.
- Authorized Admin cancellation for GUNUCO fulfilment failure uses Admin Exception with a required reason.
- Delivered: use the Returns workflow.
- Record the actor, reason, amounts, timestamp, and notifications.

Admin cancellation policy controls:
- Policy Name
- Scope: Global, Location, Parent Category, or Subcategory
- Full Refund Window Minutes, default 30
- Final Partial Refund Deadline Minutes, default 60
- Partial Refund Percentage, default 50
- Effective From and Effective To
- Active ON/OFF
- Policy preview with example booking time, deadlines, captured refund base, refund, and non-refundable amount

Owner has full authority. Admin can create and schedule policies. Branch Manager sees the effective policy read-only. Saving creates a new policy version for future bookings; existing orders retain their booking-time snapshots.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.9 REFUNDS
------------------------------------------------------------

Required columns:
- Refund ID
- Order ID
- Customer
- Payment Method
- Refund Amount
- Status
- Retry Attempts
- Initiated At
- Completed At
- Actions

Statuses:
- Pending
- Processing
- Completed
- Failed
- Manual Review

Rules:
- Refund to the original payment method where possible.
- Never refund more than the captured payment.
- Retry failed gateway refunds up to three times.
- Payment detail includes every full-payment attempt plus gateway callbacks and immutable status history.
- Cancellation detail includes Customer/Admin/System actor, policy snapshot, elapsed minutes, tier, percentage, deduction, refund amount, and correlation ID.
- Refund detail includes source cancellation or return, payment, method, idempotency key, attempts, gateway reference, failures, actor, and immutable status history.
- Move to Manual Review after the final failed retry.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.10 RETURNS
------------------------------------------------------------

Required fields:
- Order ID
- Return Reason
- Issue Description
- Photo Evidence
- Severity: Low, Medium, or High
- Proposed Resolution
- Resolution Amount
- Customer Response
- Admin Notes

Resolution options:
- Full Refund
- Partial Refund
- Replacement
- Store Credit
- Reject Return

Rules:
- Validate the configured return window.
- High-severity cases require escalation.
- Replacement creates a priority production-house order.
- Returned food products must never become sellable again.
- Returned item quantities enter Pending Disposal and require disposal method, responsible Admin, and timestamp before closure.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.11 ACCESS
------------------------------------------------------------

Web Admin Panel roles:
- Owner
- Admin
- Branch Manager

Separate application identities:
- Customer Support Agent
- Delivery Partner

Rules:
- Owner is highest and manages Admins, Branch Managers, delivery partners, branches, role permissions, and admin-location assignments.
- Admin may manage Branch Managers and delivery partners within authorized operations.
- Branch Manager requires one or more location assignments and explicit POS permission.
- Customer Support Agent signs in only to the support portal and sees ticket data plus the minimum linked-order summary read-only.
- Customer Support Agent cannot change orders, cancellation eligibility, payments, production, fulfilment, refunds, catalogue, users, or settings.
- No lower role can create, modify, suspend, or remove a higher role.
- Mobile Number is the login identifier.
- Passwords must be stored as secure hashes.
- Disabled or suspended accounts cannot log in.

Role access matrix:

```text
Area                           Owner         Admin         Branch Manager
All global controls            Full          Read-only     Read-only
Branches and admin assignment  Full          No access     No access
Menu definitions               Full          Manage        Read-only
Location menu overrides        Full          Manage        Assigned locations only
Orders and production          Full          Manage        Assigned locations only
Support Tickets                Full          All operations Assigned locations limited
POS                            Full          Authorized    Assigned locations when enabled
Pickup Order ID validation     All locations Authorized   Assigned locations only
Reports                        Full          Authorized    Assigned-location reports
```

------------------------------------------------------------
3.12 REPORTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Report groups:
- Orders by parent category, subcategory, product, and Custom Cake workflow
- Add-on quantity, revenue, discounts, and location performance
- Revenue and refunds
- Product performance
- Flavour trends
- Egg versus Eggless trends
- Sugar type trends
- Flour type trends
- Quantity and size trends
- Custom cake trends
- Cancellation and return reasons
- Delivery partner performance
- Payment reconciliation

------------------------------------------------------------
3.13 SETTINGS
------------------------------------------------------------

Sections:
- Production House Profile and Pickup Address
- Operating Hours
- Service Area
- Timezone
- Global Accept Orders
- Configurable parent-category and subcategory acceptance modes
- Custom Cakes Acceptance
- Global Daily Quota
- Category Daily Quotas
- Cake Daily Quantity Quotas
- Custom Cake Daily Quota
- Custom Cake Minimum Lead Time
- Wedding or Anniversary Cakes minimum lead time: fixed 72 hours
- Wedding or Anniversary Cakes maximum advance window: fixed 720 hours
- Eligible Cakes-subcategory Same-Day Delivery ON/OFF, cutoff, preparation lead time, slots, capacity, and service area
- Flavour Master
- Egg Preference Master: Egg and Eggless
- Sugar Type Master
- Flour Type Master: Maida and Wheat Flour
- Option Price Adjustments by Cake
- Ingredient Pricing Matrix and price-breakdown preview
- Size/Weight Master
- Standard catalogue weights fixed to 500g, 1kg, 2kg, and 3kg maximum
- Custom Cake weights through 10kg plus an Above-10kg manual quote path
- Payment Settings
- Cashless Full Payment only; no advance, installment, balance, or pay-later controls
- Full-payment verification and payment-failure alerts
- Notification Settings
- Return Window
