- Add-On Master, required/optional rules, quantity ranges, assignments, location availability, and price overrides
- Global POS and Location POS controls
- Branch feature flag, location configuration, location-category availability, and admin-location assignments

------------------------------------------------------------
3.14 GUIDED SUPPORT AND SUPPORT PANEL
------------------------------------------------------------

Guided customer support:
- Use a predefined topic menu and stored rules for Cancel Order, Payment, Pickup, Delivery, Refund, Return, Custom Cake, and Something Else.
- This feature uses normal application code and SQL only. Do not use an LLM, AI service, generated reply, or autonomous agent.
- From a signed-in order, populate Order ID, name, and phone from verified order data.
- For cancellation, evaluate booking-time policy snapshots and current server time. Show the full-refund, partial-refund, or unavailable result; do not use `Preparing` to decide eligibility.
- Guided Support cannot modify orders, mark payments, approve refunds, or override business rules.
- When guidance does not resolve the issue, show Raise Support Ticket.

Main web Admin Support Tickets:
- Add `Support Tickets` to `https://admin.gunuco.com` navigation.
- Owner and Admin see all authorized tickets. Admin has every ticket-operational control; Owner retains final authority and support-account/global-setting governance.
- Branch Manager sees tickets linked to assigned-location orders and may View, Reply, Add Internal Note, Set Open, and Set Pending only.
- Cards: Total, New, Open, Pending, Closed, Urgent, Unassigned, and Escalated.
- Filters: Ticket ID, Order ID, customer name/phone, status, priority, assigned agent, escalation owner, source, location, and date range.
- Columns: Ticket ID, Order ID, Customer, Message Preview, Priority, Status, Assigned Agent, Escalation Owner, Created At, Updated At, and Actions.
- Actions: View, Assign/Reassign/Unassign, Set Priority, Reply, Add Internal Note, Set Open, Set Pending, Escalate/Take Escalation, Close, and Reopen.
- Close requires a resolution note. Reopen requires a reason. Record the Admin actor and timestamp in immutable ticket history.
- Ticket detail includes conversation, authorized private photos, linked order snapshot, email events, assignment, escalation, notes, and complete history.
- Use authorized order/payment/refund/production/delivery screens for domain changes and store their reference in ticket history; ticket actions cannot bypass those rules.

Customer input:
- Message
- Up to 3 optional photos

Photo rules:
- Three fixed upload slots with preview and remove
- JPEG, PNG, or WebP only
- Maximum 5 MB per photo
- Validate file content, scan uploads, store privately, and authorize viewing

Ticket submission rules:
- Available from Guided Support and Application Support Form only.
- Submit from the application and email `support@gunuco.com` from the application service; never require the customer to open an email client.
- Validate that the Order ID exists and Phone Number matches the order using privacy-safe errors.
- Use an idempotency key so retrying cannot create duplicate tickets.
- Generate Ticket ID atomically in `YYMM-NN` format with a monthly sequence, for example `2608-01` and `2608-125`.
- Generate subject `Ticket {Ticket ID} | Order {Order ID}` for both mailbox and dashboard.
- On success show Ticket ID, New status, creation time, and View Ticket.

Support login:
- URL: `https://support.gunuco.com/login`
- Email, Password, Sign In, Forgot Password, and MFA when enabled
- Invalid credentials, suspended account, rate limit, session expired, and service unavailable states
- Support accounts cannot authenticate into owner or admin portals
- Admin creates one account per freelancer, sets access expiry, activates/suspends access, limits active users and concurrent sessions, and revokes access. Shared credentials are not allowed.

Support dashboard cards:
- Total Tickets
- New
- Open
- Pending
- Closed

Filters:
- Ticket ID
- Order ID
- Status
- Priority
- Assigned Agent
- Source Channel
- Date Range

Columns:
- Ticket ID
- Order ID
- Subject
- Message Preview
- Photos
- Status
- Assigned Agent
- Created At
- Last Updated At
- Actions

Ticket statuses:
- New
- Open
- Pending
- Closed

Ticket detail shows:
- Ticket ID and status
- Generated subject, customer message, and up to three photos
- Read-only minimum order summary and order-status snapshot
- Matched predefined rule and version
- Conversation timeline and internal notes
- Assigned agent and email-delivery timestamps
- Complete ticket history

Actions:
- Assign to Me
- Reassign
- Reply
- Add Internal Note
- Set Open
- Set Pending
- Escalate to Admin
- Close

Assignment rules:
- Assign new tickets transactionally to the available active agent with the fewest non-closed tickets.
- Break ties using the agent who was assigned least recently, producing an equal split for two, three, or more working agents.
- Skip suspended, expired, unavailable, or logged-out agents. Admin can reassign.

Mailbox behavior:
- Support staff can see Ticket ID, Order ID, subject, message, and permitted photos in email and the dashboard.
- Inbound email replies append to the same ticket conversation.
- Show email Pending, Sent, Received, Failed, and Bounced events. Deduplicate inbound messages by provider message ID.
- The dashboard database is the source of truth for ownership and status.

Every assignment, reply, note, status change, email, and closure is audited. Support staff cannot bypass cancellation or refund rules.

============================================================
4. DELIVERY PARTNER PANEL
============================================================

BOTTOM NAVIGATION

Orders
Earnings
Profile

This panel is mobile-first.

------------------------------------------------------------
4.1 DELIVERY ORDERS
------------------------------------------------------------

Active order fields:
- Opaque Assignment Reference; never show internal OrderID or customer-facing Order ID
- Parent Category
- Subcategory
- Product and selected Add-Ons
- Quantity
- Fragile or Custom Cake indicator
- Pickup-at-Store Address
- Customer Address and Map
- Customer Phone
- Delivery Notes
- Requested Pickup Time
- Assignment Accept-By Time

Actions:
- Accept Assignment
- Reject Assignment with Reason
- Call Customer
- Open Navigation
- Mark Picked Up
- Mark Out for Delivery
- Enter and Validate Order ID
- Mark Delivered (enabled only after a successful Order ID match)
- Report Delivery Problem

Delivery statuses:
- Pending Assignment
- Assigned
- Accepted
- Picked Up
- Out for Delivery
- Delivered
- Failed

Application behavior:
- New automatic assignments generate an in-app notification.
- Rider sees pickup time, production-house location, customer area, distance, and estimated earnings before accepting.
- Accepting reserves the assignment and updates Admin in real time.
- Rejecting requires a reason and sends the assignment back for automatic fallback.
- Rider can only update status for an assignment they accepted.
- Load rider assignments through assignment-scoped endpoints and the rider-safe projection only. Do not expose internal `OrderID` or public `PublicOrderID` in lists, details, notifications, deep links, device-visible logs, analytics payloads, validation responses, or success messages.
- The rider uses Call Customer at the destination, asks for the Order ID, enters it into a blank field, and sees only `Order confirmed` or a generic failure. Never echo the submitted, matched, or expected Order ID.

------------------------------------------------------------
4.2 EARNINGS
------------------------------------------------------------

Required items:
- Deliveries Completed Today
- Earnings Today
- Earnings This Week
- Incentives
- Payout History

------------------------------------------------------------
4.3 PROFILE
------------------------------------------------------------

Required items:
- Name
- Mobile Number
- Vehicle Number
- Rating
- Availability ON/OFF
- Accept Deliveries ON/OFF
- Support Contact

============================================================
5. ORDER STATUS MATRIX
============================================================

| Stage | Owner | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Not Accepted | Admin/System | Captured but not approved |
| Accepted | Owner/Admin/Authorized Branch Manager/System | Approved for production |
| Preparing | Production House | Cake preparation started |
| Packed | Production House | Packed for handoff |
| Ready for Delivery | Production House | Awaiting rider assignment or pickup |
| Delivery Partner Assigning | Admin/System | Assignment in progress |
| Assigned | Delivery Partner | Rider assigned |
| Picked Up | Delivery Partner | Collected from production house |
| Out for Delivery | Delivery Partner | Travelling to customer |
| Delivered | Delivery Partner | Successfully delivered |
| Cancelled | Authorized Admin/System | Cancelled before completion |
| Return Requested | Customer/Admin | Post-delivery issue raised |
| Resolved | Authorized Admin | Return or exception closed |

For `Pickup-at-Store`, the primary production status remains `Packed` while the separate pickup status moves through `Pickup Scheduled`, `Ready for Pickup`, and `Collected`. `Ready for Delivery` and all rider statuses apply only to `Doorstep-Delivery`.

============================================================
6. CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION RULES
============================================================

- Use the GUNUCO brand in every screen and notification.
- Support configurable parent categories and subcategories. Launch with Cakes and its seven approved subcategories, plus the Custom Cake workflow; keep Coffee, Pizza, and Burgers inactive.
- Treat GUNUCO PREMIUM CAKES as the curated Cakes subcategory managed by Owner or Admin.
- Admin can create future Coffee, Pizza, Burgers, and other parent categories or subcategories from Menu Management.
- Owner has full control and final authority. Admin manages definitions and operations. Branch Manager controls only authorized-location operations and menu overrides.
- The production house prepares and packs all orders.
- Every delivery starts at the production house.
- Flavour, Egg or Eggless, sugar type, flour type, size/weight, and quantity are explicit selections.
- Each eligible Cakes subcategory and product can use same-day delivery when all admin-configured capacity and timing checks pass.
- Option pricing is recalculated by the server and snapshotted on the order.
- Keep one primary order lifecycle visible in reporting.
- Returned food never becomes sellable again.
- Store reasons for rejection, cancellation, refund adjustment, return, and delivery failure.

============================================================
6A. PRODUCTION HARDENING (NO FUNCTIONALITY CHANGE)
============================================================

These controls supplement the existing screens and processes. They must not change approved roles, categories, add-ons, prices, delivery fees, quotas, statuses, fulfilment methods, or customer-visible behavior.

Server integrity:
- Use explicit server-side commands for every order, production, pickup, delivery, cancellation, refund, and return transition.
- Validate current state, role, active account, assigned location, POS permission, fulfilment method, and completed payment for every command. Validate rider assignment for local Doorstep-Delivery commands and courier shipment ownership/state for Nationwide-Delivery commands.
- Commit Order ID allocation, quote snapshots, quota/slot reservation, payment confirmation, order creation, audit history, and outbox events in one atomic booking transaction.
- Use concurrency-safe quota and slot reservations and optimistic concurrency for editable admin records.
- Record previous/new order, pickup, and delivery states with actor, reason, correlation ID, and timestamp.

Payment integrity:
- Attach an idempotency key to checkout, full-payment, and refund requests. Retrying the same request returns the original result.
- Treat gateway return screens as Processing until a signature-verified webhook or authoritative gateway lookup confirms payment.
- Ignore duplicate provider event IDs safely and reconcile captured, refunded, and order amounts.
- Use INR fixed-decimal calculations and documented two-decimal rounding; never use floating point for money.

UI states:
- Disable repeated submission while a command is pending and reuse the original idempotency key for retry.
- Provide loading, empty, permission-denied, stale-data conflict, external-service failure, retry, and offline states.
- Preserve form data after recoverable failures.
- For stale updates, show `Record changed by another user` and `Review Latest`; never silently overwrite.
- Confirm destructive and financial actions and show a correlation/reference ID in the result.

Security and operations:
- Require MFA for Owner and support session expiration, revocation, secure reset, and rate limiting.
- Rate-limit login, password reset, Order ID validation, quote, route, payment, and upload endpoints.
- Validate and malware-scan uploads; use private storage and short-lived signed URLs.
- Process notifications, rider assignment, gateway follow-up, refunds, and integration events through a transactional outbox and retryable workers.
- Monitor payment-without-order, quota conflicts, stuck orders, assignment exhaustion, repeated validation failures, refund failures, route failures, webhook failures, and outbox backlog.
- Use versioned migrations, encrypted point-in-time backups, restore drills, and documented recovery objectives.

Release verification:
- Test every role/location boundary, state transition, full-payment path, fulfilment method, category module, add-on rule, cancellation, refund, and return.
- Test concurrent final-quota checkout, duplicate callbacks, simultaneous edits, annual sequence allocation, and rider reassignment.
- Complete security, accessibility, load, reconciliation, provider-failure, and backup-restore testing before launch.

============================================================
7. LOCATION AND FUTURE CATEGORY READINESS
============================================================

Branches remain feature-disabled at launch, but the implementation includes the location contract from the first release:
- Owner-only branch creation and activation behind a feature flag
- Branch Manager role and location-scoped authorization
- Category, subcategory, product, add-on, quota, POS, order, fulfilment, and reporting records tied to location
- Server-selected order location; never trust an unrestricted client location value
- Disabling a location or its POS blocks new activity while preserving history

Admin can add future categories and subcategories without a migration. Coffee, Pizza, Burgers, and other names are examples only and must not be hard-coded. Their product modules use configurable schemas and do not require cake-only fields.

============================================================
8. FINAL DELIVERY NOTE
============================================================

Use this document with `END_TO_END_WORKFLOW.md`, `UI_WIREFRAME_REFERENCE.md`, and `tables.sql` as the implementation handoff. All four files describe the same current production-house-only model.